course: dictionary
lesson: 4966
title: Incite: stirring people up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To incite means to stir people up, or to urge them, so that they want to do something bad or violent, or feel angry. Think of it as pushing people towards trouble.
explain: Be careful: incite is not the same as excite. Taffy writes «inciting» when she means exciting, which is a mix-up. Excite means to make someone feel happy and eager, but incite means pushing people towards harm or anger. Good phrases to remember are incite violence, incite a riot and incite hatred.
explain: Words can incite, so think about what your words might make other people do. In law, to incite someone is to urge them to commit a crime, and that urging can be a crime too.
fact: Incite means to stir up or encourage people to do something bad or violent, or to feel angry.
fact: In law, to incite someone means to urge them to commit a crime, and inciting a crime can itself be a crime.
fact: Incite is not the same as excite: excite means to make someone feel happy and eager.
fact: Common phrases are incite violence, incite a riot and incite hatred.
fact: Writers can also use «inciting» for things that are not people, such as smells that stir up feelings in an animal's nose.
exercise: Which word means to stir people up to do something bad? | Excite | Calm | Soothe | *Incite
exercise: Taffy writes «inciting» when she means exciting. What is the right word for her meaning? | Incite | Invite | *Excite | Ignore
exercise: Which phrase uses incite correctly? | Incite a birthday | *Incite a riot | Incite a nap | Incite a picnic
test: In the writer's words «summoning, warning, inciting, repelling», what does inciting mean? | Giving a gift | Washing away | Putting to sleep | *Stirring up or prompting a feeling
test: In law, what does it mean to incite someone to commit a crime? | Reporting the crime to a teacher | *Urging them to commit the crime | Forgiving the crime | Helping them hide from the police
exam: Which sentence uses incite correctly? | *Words can incite people to hatred and harm | He incited a cup of tea | The rain incited the picnic | The puppy was incited to sleep
